# Line endings are settled here rather than per-machine, so a checkout on
# Windows, macOS and Linux produces byte-identical files. Without this, a
# Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true rewrites every file to CRLF and Git
# then announces it on every command, and the .githooks/commit-msg shell script
# would not even run there (`sh` rejects a CRLF shebang line).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never normalize and never diff as text. Winnower handles images all day, and
# a test fixture or README screenshot corrupted by line-ending conversion is a
# confusing way to lose an afternoon.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.zip  binary
